-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]


An unconfigured device gets its IP address via DHCP, Login username and password is 'ubnt'. Once the device has been adopted by a controller, it will use the device password of the 'Site config' page. Use ssh to login.

  - Login
  - possibly backup the stock firmware using <code>
dd if=/dev/mtd2ro of=/tmp/jffs.img
</code>
  - scp /tmp/jffs.img to your backup location, rm /tmp/jffs.img from the device to save memory
  - Download the factory.bin image as shown above
  - scp the image to the /tmp directory of your device
  - Install OpenWrt using <code>
fwupdate.real -m openwrt-ar71xx-generic-ubnt-unifi-outdoor-plus-squashfs-factory.bin -d
</code>

